  "title": "Counting maps from 3-manifold groups into S3 is #P-hard, and doubles count pairs of colourings",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups into small non-abelian groups",
  "conclusion": "Counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups into S3 is #P-hard: handlebodies with tori attached along a planar graph turn it into a spin model that recovers 3-colourings, and their closed doubles count pairs of colourings, 2 P(G,9)/3^|V|. The same holds on closed manifolds for most dihedral groups, Q8 and A4, so for class-2 targets bounded H2 is needed.",
